            <div xml:id="d101">

                <pb facs="0100" n="94" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg94"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.60D/112a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Finland</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-16T17:00:00-04:00">November 16,
                            1942—5 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>225. We see no objection to your actively circulating among such persons as you
                    think appropriate, the statements that we consider Witting and his Ministry so
                    pro-German that we expect nothing but a continuous worsening of relations with
                    Finland as long as he remains in office and that it is out of the question to
                    expect any <hi rendition="#italic">rapprochement</hi> with the United States
                    until he is replaced by a person in whom we can have some confidence.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
